<http://example.org/sen0414-ch2125corr-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 21 to 25 corrections"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch2125corr_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.0.0 (2026-11-26): Mission stage only (one stage per version). Opened on the owner's instructions of 2026-11-26: 18:57 Istanbul ("after 16-20, the next is the 21-25. After the completion we will return back to initial chapters"), recorded as a queued lineage in register 1.21.0 of Lineage13 (route c of the Lineage Operating Discipline v163.0.7, 3g), and 20:18 Istanbul ("Fine, proceed"), given after Lineage13 closed. READING OF THE INSTRUCTION, stated so it can be corrected: the mission is the same slice as Lineage13 for the next five chapters, chapters 21 to 25. After this lineage the owner returns to the initial chapters; that return is a further queued lineage and is not part of this one.
ORDINAL AND ONE-AT-A-TIME CHECK: the live register files were read on 2026-11-26. Lineage13 (chapters 16 to 20) is LS_Achieved and archived (register 1.40.0, archive v1_1_0, closure report in 07-lineage). Lineage12, Lineage11 and Lineage10 are archived; Lineages 4 to 9 are LS_Achieved. Lineage3 (chapters 9 and 10) still reads LS_InProgress in its own register, as it did when Lineages 4 to 13 opened; it is a finding for the initial-chapters work and is not run or touched here. The highest ordinal in the register and its archives is 13; the next free ordinal is 14.
OE CEREMONY: the rules governing this stage were read from the highest OE governance ABox on GitHub (oegov_abox_v1_56_0.ttl, oe-method 3.178.0): BP-D2 (read the bytes, not a summary), BP-D7 and BP-D62 (a changed file gets a new version), BP-D63 and B8 (plain talk with the owner), L-64 (stay in own scope), L-65 and L-66 (verify by re-reading, use declared measurements), L-78 (act when rules and evidence decide), L-113 (every named item gets its own disposition), L-114 (append corrections), L-118 (labels before identifiers). Enforcement: backlog_next_act check before every step, one commit per stage, git as the witness of order. The Lineage Operating Discipline v163.0.7 and the Lineage Practice Guide v1.0.0 were fetched from GitHub the same day (BRSF 5.5.26).
VERIFIED GAPS (live files measured 2026-11-26 with gap_measure_v1_0_0.py, logs gap_measure.log and gap_measure_pages.log in 08-tooling/lineage14-opening): chapters 21 to 25 each have a first-version deck of 26 slides (08-tooling/chNN-deck/sen0414_chNN_deck_v1_0_0.pptx; none is in the chapter folder under 03-materials) and a page of version 9.35.0 as the newest. Decks: 0 of the code slides carry two result balloons in each of the five; '>>>' prompts appear in the slide text 67, 39, 39, 38 and 45 times; the word lambda appears 11, 9, 3, 9 and 1 times; phrases of the think-of kind 1, 0, 2, 0 and 0 times; the reader-notes check reports 12, 15, 21, 14 and 17 findings; fit, overlap and story-prose checks are clean on all five; 0 analogy-marked slides; every slide has notes. Pages: the newest page of each chapter has no run-in-order menu item, no page A-box file and no chapter-code manifest exists in the chapter folder, no page test log exists, each page carries 33 '>>>' prompts and the word lambda 231, 194, 1167, 179 and 166 times (counted in the whole page file, scripts included). The decks are not yet measured against deck standard 1.3.0, which needs a chapter-code manifest that does not exist.
NOT MEASURED YET (named, not dropped): deck standard 1.3.0 and the material check on the five decks and pages, whether the five pages pass the full page test on the current pipeline, whether the chapter code, the page and the lab libraries carry matching code, whether story pictures and links of chapters 21 to 25 are current, and the story-repeat check over chapters 21 to 25 against all others. They are measured in the scope stage before any goal rests on them.
WHY A NEW LINEAGE: Lineage13 is closed and archived, and a closed lineage is revived only in extraordinary cases; chapters 21 to 25 are a different closeable slice, the next in the owner's order.
REDUCING REWORK: the conversion of Lineages 10 to 13 is reused, not rebuilt: each deck is rebuilt once through the generic chapter builder from a spec and each page through the lambda-free A-box maker and the page test. Chapters 21 to 25 start from first-version decks, so each needs a spec and a chapter-code manifest first, which the earlier chapters already had."""@en,
        "1.1.0 (2026-11-26): Scope stage only (one stage per version): the scope statement with its areas, deliverables and exclusions, derived from the Mission stage's verified gaps (Lineage Operating Discipline v163.0.7, 3d). The shape rules that earlier scope stages found only on a second pass are answered at once (each area has a location, a counted measure and a layer; each deliverable a layer and a quoted mission clause; each exclusion a concern, a layer and a decision-maker). Measured here: the material check on the five old decks and pages (6 of 8 conditions fail on each, logs material_ch*.log) and a first read of the story-repeat log (no story repeat found for chapters 21 to 25; shared names only: Fredrik Lundh in chapters 21 and 18, Bell Labs in chapter 24 and chapters 5, 8 and 19; to be re-read after the rebuild). The page test, matching code and links stay scope items measured before any goal rests on them. Lesson of Lineage13 taken: an exclusion names the act it forbids exactly (modifying or deleting an existing file), and the folders allowed to change are listed in the scope text."@en,
        "1.2.0 (2026-11-26): Goal stage only (one stage per version). Derived from Scope14, not from a list of gaps (Lineage Operating Discipline v163.0.7, 3d): one mission-facing goal; scope-facing goals that between them cover all nine areas; one containment-facing goal; one exclusion-facing goal for each of the five exclusions. Each goal states the benefit of what the work implements; the conditions of the record are measured by the objectives of the next stage."@en,
        "1.24.0 (2026-11-27): chapter 25 spec and build done; Spec_25 Done, Deck_25_1 Done, Deck_25_2 InProgress"@en,
        "1.3.0 (2026-11-26): Objective stage only (one stage per version). Each goal is measured by objectives (27 in all), each metric derived from its goal, each with a counted, derived or judged measurement and a query that reads it, a baseline measured on 2026-11-26 (logs gap_measure.log, gap_measure_pages.log and material_ch*.log in 08-tooling/lineage14-opening/) and a baseline observation. Objectives whose figure is met by absence carry the direction Hold. Lessons of Lineage13 taken: no target is a count of something that can be miscounted (the balloon objective counts the examples that lack balloons, 42 today, down to 0; an objective that cannot be read yet says so in its query); the rdodi objective counts existing files modified or deleted; the allowed folders of the outside-files objective are listed in its query; the judged content objective names the recorded-paragraph case Lineage13 counted. CORRECTION OF THE MISSION STAGE 1.0.0 (appended, never edited): it said that the slide text holds '>>>' prompts 67, 39, 39, 38 and 45 times; those are occurrences of the three characters, of which 26 per deck are a lone mark shape on every slide and the rest are prompt lines of code (41, 13, 13, 12 and 19). The new objective DeckPrompts counts all of them. The objectives are written by the table script 08-tooling/lineage14-opening/objective_make_v1_0_0.py, the lineage's own script (a BRSF handover is owed with the others)."@en,
        "1.4.0 (2026-11-26): Backlog stage of Lineage14: the register root, the backlog, 26 stories with acceptance criteria and links to the objectives they move and the deliverables they satisfy, and the lineage's own Definition of Done. Tasks follow in the planning stage, where each is produced by a planning event. CORRECTION OF 1.3.0 (appended, never edited): the spec objective of 1.3.0 said that none of the five chapters has a spec folder and set the target at 5. Both were wrong: specs exist (chapter 16 spec_v4_0_0, chapter 17 spec_v4_0_0, chapter 18 spec_v3_0_0, chapter 19 spec, chapter 20 spec_v2_0_1) and the newest decks were built from them by the generic builder versions 2.9.0, 2.6.0, 2.4.0, 2.2.0 and 2.3.0. The baseline 0 stays true read as chapters whose newest deck is built by the current generic builder 2.10.0; the target is 3, the chapters 21 to 25 that are re-cut, because chapters 16 and 17 need no re-cut (mission: reduce rework). The wrong text stays visible in 1.3.0."@en,
        "1.5.0 (2026-11-26): Planning stage of Lineage14: five packages (one per chapter, the last also carrying the measurement and closing stories), five time-boxed iterations that match them, and the planning of the first iteration only (refinement, planning events, typed tasks). Iterations 2 to 5 are planned when they start, by small steps. Dates are forecasts, never deadlines."@en,
        "1.6.0 (2026-11-26): Merged register. Deltas 1.0.0 to 1.5.0 combined into one file; hasState, hasLineageStatus, hasMissionOutcome, checkpointDate, hasForecastDate, hasForecastRationale, hasTargetValue, metricTarget and expectedValue take their latest value; every other statement is kept. Moves recorded here: the lineage is In progress, story ST14_Spec_21 and its first task are InProgress (iteration 1 starts). Made by the lineage's own script register_step_v1_1_0.py (Lineage14 copy)."@en,
        "1.7.0 (2026-11-26): TK14_Spec_21_1 Done, TK14_Spec_21_2 InProgress; owner's deck-shape decision recorded as an audit note."@en,
        "1.8.0 (2026-11-26): Spec_21 tasks and story Done; Deck_21_1 Done; Deck_21 story and Deck_21_2 InProgress; deck 4.0.0 built and checked."@en,
        "Chapter 21 released: Deck_21, Release_21 Done"@en,
        "Chapter 22 released"@en,
        "Chapter 22 spec and build done, deck stage started"@en,
        "Chapter 23 released: Deck_23, Page_23, Release_23 Done"@en,
        "Chapter 23 spec and build done, deck stage started"@en,
        "Iteration 2 (chapter 22) planned and started"@en,
        "Iteration 2 stories Done"@en,
        "Iteration 3 (chapter 23) planned and started"@en,
        "Iteration 4 (chapter 24) planned and started"@en,
        "Iteration 5 (chapter 25) planned and started"@en,
        "Page_21 Done, Deck_21_2 Done, Deck_21_3 InProgress"@en,
        "TK14_Page_21_1 InProgress; Page_21 story InProgress"@en,
        "TK14_Spec_22_1 Done, TK14_Spec_22_2 InProgress"@en,
        "chapter 24 released"@en,
        "chapter 24 spec Done, deck 4.0.0 built and checked"@en ;
    owl:priorVersion <http://example.org/sen0414-ch2125corr-lineage/1.23.0> ;
    owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch2125corr-lineage/1_24_0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "1_24_0" .

ex:Blueprint14 a backlog:Blueprint ;
