ex:DoD14 a backlog:DefinitionOfDone ;
    rdfs:label "Definition of Done of the chapters 21 to 25 corrections lineage"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage14 ;
    backlog:hasDoDCriterion ex:DoD14_ContentUnchanged,
        ex:DoD14_DeckChecks,
        ex:DoD14_MatchingCode,
        ex:DoD14_MaterialCheck,
        ex:DoD14_OutsideFiles,
        ex:DoD14_OwnVersion,
        ex:DoD14_PageTest,
        ex:DoD14_ReviewRecord,
        ex:DoD14_RunOrderShape,
        ex:DoD14_StoryRepeat ;
    rdfs:comment "Written for this lineage. A story is Done only when each acceptance criterion has a check run in the current turn with its output saved in the repository, a verify task re-runs it from the files and not from the builder's report, and a check that cannot be run or a result that is not shown leaves the story open." .

ex:Lineage14 a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 21 to 25 corrections, narrow lineage"@en ;
    backlog:continuesFrom ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:followsProfileDeclaration ex:ProfileDecl14 ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "1.18.0 (2026-11-27): chapter 23 spec and build done, deck stage started. Deck 4.0.0 has 41 slides (the owner's shape of chapters 12 to 20, about 34 to 40, is exceeded by one: the concept tables of the three long parts needed a second slide each so that no table runs off the slide); 15 examples ran on a private virtual display, never on a real screen, Windows or macOS; the story of cut, copy and paste was replaced by Control-Alt-Delete because chapter 8 already tells the Tesler story; the CAPTCHA story (coining of the word, 2003) sits beside chapter 22's reCAPTCHA story (2009) and is disclosed. Seven deck checks zero; GitHub link to PyAutoGUI could not be opened from the session (403 from the access policy).",
        "1.19.0 (2026-11-27): chapter 23 released - deck 4.0.0 (41 slides), page 9.110.0 (416 pass, 0 fail, 104 of 104 widgets), page shapes conform, material check clean with no lambda on the page, 74 of 74 A-box inputs equal, review record (12 verdicts) and release record in 07-lineage/reports. Faults and limits are listed in the release record: the concept tables were split (builder 2.11.0), the cut-copy-paste story was replaced because chapter 8 tells it, the lab observer lambdas were rewritten, the page shows all 15 examples as recorded, the examples ran on a virtual display only, one GitHub link could not be opened from the session.",
        "1.20.0 (2026-11-27): iteration 4 (chapter 24) planned with typed tasks from the scope tree and started; first task InProgress. Iteration 3 (chapter 23) closed: its stories are Done since 1.19.0.",
        "1.23.0 (2026-11-27): iteration 5 (chapter 25) planned with typed tasks from the scope tree and started; first task InProgress. Iteration 4 (chapter 24) closed: its stories are Done since 1.22.0.",
        "1.24.0 (2026-11-27): chapter 25 spec and build done, deck stage started. Deck 4.0.0 has 42 slides (the owner's shape of chapters 12 to 20, about 34 to 40, is exceeded by two: seven concept slides, because the 49 research concepts need at most twelve rows a slide); 17 examples ran for real under Python 3.14.6 and the free-threaded build of Python 3.14.6 (programs that wait print only lists, names, errors, counts and booleans; the downloader asks a local stand-in and xkcd.com is never contacted); the recorded timings are those of 2026-10-14, marked Recorded, and the five-interpreter table was probed live (Python 3.11 to 3.13 were installed for it with uv). Five stories with sourced pictures, one for each of parts 2 to 5 and two for part 3; part 1 has none because no sourced picture of the first choice (Corbato, CTSS) was found on Commons; the Munroe story shares the person with chapter 16's Bobby Tables story (a different story, disclosed); the Therac, Dijkstra and blackout pictures are the first version's recorded Commons copies. Seven deck checks zero; all 13 resource links answered 200 on 2026-11-27 (one after a retry following a 429).",
        "2026-11-26: chapter 21 spec Done and deck 4.0.0 built (03-materials/ch21/SEN0414_Ch21_GraphsAndImages_3e_v4_0_0.pptx, 40 slides, 15 code slides, 6 story slides with sourced pictures whose licences are in 03-materials/ch21/assets/story_images_v1_0_0.json). Deck checks: standard 13 of 13, fit, layout, overlap, reader notes, story prose and notes all clean (logs in 08-tooling/ch21-deck/logs_v4_0_0); phrase hits 0, lambda 0, prompts 0 (first version: 78 lambda or prompt occurrences). TK14_Deck_21_2 stays InProgress: the material check needs the new page, which is the next stage. Disclosures: the examples run under Python 3.12.3 with Pillow 13.0.0, Matplotlib 3.11.2 and NumPy 2.5.5, not the 3.14.6 of the first version; the clipboard example is emulated; LibreOffice rendering only.",
        "2026-11-26: owner decision (answer to the question on deck length): the decks of chapters 21 to 25 take the same shape as chapters 12 to 20 (parts, concept slides in plain words, stories with sourced pictures, one code slide for each example with two result balloons, a native table, practice, summary and resources), about 40 slides; this overrides the earlier ruling of no added slides for these chapters, because their first-version decks are of an older, shorter shape. TK14_Spec_21_1 (analysis) Done: the first-version examples fetched the publisher's zip, whose licence is open and whose site answered 429 on 2026-11-26, so the new examples of chapter 21 draw their own pictures and need no book file; the clipboard of pyperclipimg needs a display and is emulated by a class with the same two calls, as the slide says; the first-version deck stays unchanged.",
        "2026-11-26: the lineage status was not advanced stage by stage while the chain was built (Mission, Scope, Goal, Objective, Backlog); the commits of 1.0.0 to 1.4.0 are the witness of that order. The status pointer (one value, moved in place) and the story and task states are moved in the next merged register, because a delta file only adds statements and a second value would break the single-value rules; until then the lineage pointer still reads Opened and every item reads Proposed.",
        "2026-11-27: chapter 24 released - deck 4.0.0 (42 slides), page 9.111.0 (412 of 412 page-test features, 104 of 104 widgets, shapes conform, material check 8 of 8, no lambda on the page, 74 of 74 lambda-free A-box inputs equal), stories 2.0.1 (story-repeat control clean), page builder 4.19.0, review record (12 verdicts: accept 10, accept with limits 2) and release record in 07-lineage/reports. Logs in 08-tooling/lineage14-opening/ch24_deck_4_0_0 and ch24_page_9_111_0. Disclosures: examples ran on this machine only (no sound card, Windows or macOS); the Internet Archive reading stands in for YouTube and nothing was downloaded from it; three GitHub resource links answered 403 from the session's access policy; the deck has 42 slides above the agreed about 34 to 40; the page shows all 16 chapter examples as recorded; owner has not opened deck or page; LibreOffice rendering only; build environments gained packages and apt tools, two extra Python environments and a path link. Tool gaps owed to BRSF: register step, planner, page-input makers, lambda-free A-box makers, lecture exports, spec builders, lab helper, page builder 4.19.0.",
        "2026-11-27: chapter 24 spec Done and deck 4.0.0 built (03-materials/ch24/SEN0414_Ch24_MakePythonTalk_3e_v4_0_0.pptx, 42 slides, 16 code slides, 6 story slides with sourced pictures whose licences are in 03-materials/ch24/assets/story_images_v1_0_0.json). Deck checks: standard 13 of 13, fit, layout, overlap, reader notes, story prose and notes all clean (logs in 08-tooling/lineage14-opening/ch24_deck_4_0_0); lambda 0, prompts 0 (first version: 47 occurrences); story-repeat control clean (two shared institution names, different stories, read). TK14_Deck_24_2 stays InProgress: the material check needs the new page, which is the next stage. Disclosures: examples ran on this machine only (no sound card, no Windows or macOS), archive.org reading stands in for YouTube and nothing was downloaded from YouTube; 13 of 16 resource links opened, the three GitHub pages answered 403 through the shell (two are named as source by the package pages on PyPI); story facts read from Wikipedia HTML pages; picture files fetched in standard thumbnail sizes after Wikimedia rate limits; slide count 42 is above the agreed 34 to 40; LibreOffice rendering only.",
        "Chapter 21 page 9.107.0 built from the generic template 9.55.0: lambda-free domain A-box 1.0.3 (61 of 61 results equal to 1.0.2, 0 lambdas), stories file 1.0.1 (the deck's six stories, ids and facts unchanged, titles of two aligned, a personal address removed from its link-check header), stand-in 1.0.2 (PyplotState shown as recorded because plt.show() prints a browser warning), run-in-order item present. Page test 416 passed, 0 failed on the third run; the first run failed on that plt.show() warning (fixed), the second on an outside HTTP 429 of the semantic-search model and one load-timing bound (nothing changed, test re-run), logs kept. Page-shapes check conforms; material check of deck 4.0.0 with the page passes, so Deck_21_2 closes. Disclosed: the book's chapter page answered HTTP 429 when the resource links were re-read (14 of 15 answered 200), so the deck's 'opened on 2026-11-26' holds for 14 links; the examples were recorded under Python 3.13.18 or 3.12.3 with Pillow 13.0.0, not 3.14.6 with Pillow 12.3.0.",
        "Chapter 21 page stage starts. The deck 4.0.0 is built and its checks are clean; its material check needs the new page and so closes after the page is built (task Deck_21_2 stays InProgress for that reason). The chapter 21 domain A-box v1.0.2 holds 61 examples written as one-expression lambda wrappers; a lambda-free version is made as a new file, as for chapters 19 and 20.",
        "Chapter 21 released. The three-role reading found that the page's Lecture tab still described the first-version deck; a lecture file for deck 4.0.0 (40 slides) was made and the page rebuilt as 9.108.0 (page 9.107.0 stays as the earlier version): page test 416 passed, 0 failed on its first run, page shapes conform, material check clean, version check exit 0. Twelve verdicts recorded (accept 10, accept with limits 2) in REVIEW_RECORD_ch21_Lineage14_v1_0_0.md; release record REPORT_Lineage14_ch21_release_and_review_v1_0_0.md names the released versions and the limits (LibreOffice rendering only; Python 3.12.3 and 3.13.18 with Pillow 13.0.0 instead of 3.14.6 with 12.3.0; the book's own chapter page not re-read because of HTTP 429; the owner has not opened deck or page).",
        "Chapter 22 (Recognizing Text) read for the spec: the first-version deck has 26 slides with console sessions and 12 programs, the chapter corpus has 73 input-output examples and 39 research concepts that each need a plain-word row, six stories exist (Goldberg1915, Goldberg1931, Kurzweil1976, Tesseract1985, Recaptcha2009, Frankenstein1831) and the first-version page shows 66 of its examples as recorded because a browser has no Tesseract. The spec carries: 15 examples that run here with the real Tesseract 5.3.4 (pytesseract 0.3.13, Pillow, OpenCV), draw their own pictures and use no book file, no lambda and no prompt; the screen is a picture drawn by the program (pyautogui needs a display) and NAPS2 is not installed, so its command is built and the missing program is shown through the error subprocess raises. On the page the examples that call Tesseract are shown as recorded with their reason; the others run. Six story pictures must be sourced from Wikimedia Commons (rate limits expected).",
        "Chapter 22 released: deck 4.0.0 (38 slides), page 9.109.0 test 416/0 on the third run (causes of the first two kept), shapes conform, material check clean, story-repeat control clean, review record with 12 verdicts and release report written. Limits: LibreOffice rendering only; 14 of 15 examples recorded in the page; two GitHub resource links unverifiable from this session.",
        "Chapter 22 spec 4.0.0 written; generic builder 2.10.0 built a 38-slide deck; seven deck checks all zero; comparison log with first-version deck saved (48 lambda or >>> occurrences before, 0 now); 15 examples run with real Tesseract 5.3.4 under Python 3.12.3; story pictures sourced, Goldberg stone licence is Copyrighted free use and the reCAPTCHA picture is only 250 by 47 px; environment change disclosed: rdflib, pyshacl and requests added to the build environment.",
        "Iteration 2 (chapter 22) closed: its four stories Done with proof in the release record and report of 2026-11-27.",
        "Iteration 2 (chapter 22) starts after the release of chapter 21 (register 1.11.0). Planned with the same four stories and eleven typed tasks as iteration 1 (spec, deck, page, release); the deck takes the shape of chapters 12 to 20 (about 34 slides) as the owner decided on 2026-11-26.",
        "Iteration 3 (chapter 23) planned with typed tasks from the scope tree and started; first task InProgress." ;
